{"verdict":"All four sample answers are correct, short and grounded, and clean() already guards times and drawn days. A rule that calls days before the first listed day 'unknown' will break weekend and holiday questions, a mid-line cut of the facts can fake a short day, and several guards and line rules leave room for drawn repetition or unchecked dates.","findings":[{"severity":"high","what":"The facts start from today, so a gap between Now and the first listed day (a weekend, a holiday) means no classes. The prompt instead tells the model those dates are unknown and that it must never say they have no classes. On a Saturday, '這週末要上課嗎' gets a refusal or a hedge instead of 不用上課.","evidence":"Prompt: “The facts below are their classes from today on … Dates before the first or after the last listed day are unknown: never say they have no classes.” None of the examples has a Now that falls before the first listed day.","fix":"State that any unlisted date from today to the last listed day has no classes, including dates before the first listed day. Only dates after the last listed day are unknown."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Facts are cut at 4,500 characters, which can split a line mid-day. The last day then looks complete but shorter, so questions like 最早放學 or 有幾節 return a wrong day or count with full confidence. clean() also accepts that partial day as drawable.","evidence":"input(): “const facts = String(raw?.facts || '').slice(0, 4500);”. The day regex in clean() matches a truncated line just as well.","fix":"When the facts are too long, cut them at the last full line."},{"severity":"medium","what":"The line rules contradict each other. One tells the model to say when school ends; another says never to list times. The result is lines that repeat what the drawn periods already show (the period number) and skip the glance-level insight (that it is today, this afternoon).","evidence":"Prompt: “Say what the drawn periods don’t show at a glance (e.g. when school ends…)” vs “The app draws the times and subjects: never list them in line.” Example 1 line: “下次體育課是11/11（週三）第5節，在室外上課。”: 第5節 is the highlighted period, and it never says it is 今天.","fix":"Ban listing period numbers, times and subjects in the line, but allow one summing-up time (when school ends, when the next class starts). Have the model say 今天/明天 for today and tomorrow."},{"severity":"medium","what":"Dates and weekdays in the line are never checked. A cheap model that works out a weekday itself (11/13（週四）) ships a wrong fact the reader will trust. Clock times written in words (下午2點, 2pm) also slip past the HH:MM check.","evidence":"clean(): “(Times must be the timetable's own; counts and dates the AI may say.)”. Only /\d{1,2}:\d{2}/ is checked, while the prompt asks for “never 下午2點 or 2:00”.","fix":"In clean(), reject a line whose M/D（週X） or 'Thu M/D' weekday disagrees with the facts' line for that date. Also reject digit+點 and am/pm times."},{"severity":"low","what":"The time whitelist includes the Now time, which is not a class time. A line such as '10:30上課' would pass the check.","evidence":"clean(): “const have = new Set(times(facts)…)”, where the facts' first line is “Now: 2026-11-11 (Wed) 10:30.”","fix":"Build the whitelist from the facts without the Now line."}],"edits":[{"old":"A date missing between the first and last listed day has no classes. Dates before the first or after the last listed day are unknown: never say they have no classes.","new":"Any date from today (the Now line) to the last listed day that has no line of its own has no classes (weekend, holiday), including days before the first listed day. Only dates after the last listed day are unknown: never say they have no classes.","why":"The facts start today, so a gap before the first listed day is a day off, not an unknown. This fixes weekend and holiday answers."},{"old":"const facts = String(raw?.facts || '').slice(0, 4500);","new":"const all = String(raw?.facts || ''); const facts = all.length > 4500 ? all.slice(0, 4500).replace(/\n[^\n]*$/, '') : all;","why":"Never hand the model, or clean()'s day map, a half day that looks like an early dismissal."},{"old":"The app draws the times and subjects: never list them in line.","new":"The app draws each period’s number, time and subject: never list them in line; one summing-up time (when school ends, when the next class starts) is fine.","why":"Removes the contradiction with 'when school ends' and stops the line repeating the highlighted period number."},{"old":"the answer first, no markdown.","new":"the answer first, no markdown. For today or tomorrow write 今天/明天 (English: today/tomorrow) instead of the date.","why":"Whether it is today or tomorrow is the glance-level insight the drawn date row doesn't give quickly (Example 1)."},{"old":"const have = new Set(times(facts).map(t => t.padStart(5, '0')));","new":"const have = new Set(times(facts.replace(/^Now:.*$/m, '')).map(t => t.padStart(5, '0')));","why":"Only class times may appear in the line; the current clock time is not one."},{"old":"if (!a || !times(a).every(t => have.has(t.padStart(5, '0')))) return null;","new":"if (!a || !times(a).every(t => have.has(t.padStart(5, '0')))) return null;
      // (No clock time in words; a written weekday must be the facts' own.)
      if (/\d\s*點|\b\d{1,2}\s*(?:am|pm)\b/i.test(a)) return null;
      const wk = { Mon: '一', Tue: '二', Wed: '三', Thu: '四', Fri: '五', Sat: '六', Sun: '日' };
      const dow = new Map([...facts.matchAll(/^\d{4}-(\d{2})-(\d{2}) (\w{3}):/gm)].map(m => [`${+m[1]}/${+m[2]}`, m[3]]));
      if ([...a.matchAll(/(\d{1,2})\/(\d{1,2})（週(.)）/g)].some(m => dow.has(`${+m[1]}/${+m[2]}`) && wk[dow.get(`${+m[1]}/${+m[2]}`)] !== m[3])) return null;
      if ([...a.matchAll(/\b(Mon|Tue|Wed|Thu|Fri|Sat|Sun) (\d{1,2})\/(\d{1,2})/g)].some(m => dow.has(`${+m[2]}/${+m[3]}`) && dow.get(`${+m[2]}/${+m[3]}`) !== m[1])) return null;","why":"Code can check what the prompt only asks for: weekdays copied from the facts and no invented clock formats."}],"examples":[{"name":"weekend before first listed day","input":"{"question":"這週末要上課嗎？","facts":"Now: 2026-11-14 (Sat) 09:00.\n2026-11-16 Mon: 1 08:10-09:00 數學; 2 09:10-10:00 國文; 3 10:10-11:00 英文; 4 11:10-12:00 物理; 5 13:10-14:00 化學; 6 14:10-15:00 音樂; 7 15:10-16:00 體育 (outdoors)\n2026-11-17 Tue: 1 08:10-09:00 英文; 2 09:10-10:00 數學; 3 10:10-11:00 地理; 4 11:10-12:00 國文; 5 13:10-14:00 生物"}","expect":"Says plainly that there are no classes this weekend (11/14–11/15), with show []. It may mention that classes resume 11/16（週一）. It must not say the weekend is unknown or that the timetable doesn't show it."},{"name":"today's dismissal, late afternoon","input":"{"question":"今天幾點放學？","facts":"Now: 2026-11-11 (Wed) 15:20.\n2026-11-11 Wed: 1 08:10-09:00 國文; 2 09:10-10:00 英文; 3 10:10-11:00 數學; 4 11:10-12:00 物理; 5 13:10-14:00 體育 (outdoors); 6 14:10-15:00 歷史; 7 15:10-16:00 自習\n2026-11-12 Thu: 1 08:10-09:00 數學; 2 09:10-10:00 化學; 3 10:10-11:00 英文; 4 11:10-12:00 國文; 5 13:10-14:00 地理; 6 14:10-15:00 美術"}","expect":"Line says 今天 and 16:00, written exactly as 16:00 (never 下午4點 or 4:00). show is [{day 2026-11-11, periods [7]}]. No other times."},{"name":"current class counts in this-week total","input":"{"question":"這週還有幾節數學？","facts":"Now: 2026-11-11 (Wed) 10:30.\n2026-11-11 Wed: 1 08:10-09:00 國文; 2 09:10-10:00 英文; 3 10:10-11:00 數學; 4 11:10-12:00 物理; 5 13:10-14:00 體育 (outdoors); 6 14:10-15:00 歷史; 7 15:10-16:00 自習\n2026-11-12 Thu: 1 08:10-09:00 數學; 2 09:10-10:00 化學; 3 10:10-11:00 英文; 4 11:10-12:00 國文; 5 13:10-14:00 地理; 6 14:10-15:00 美術\n2026-11-13 Fri: 1 08:10-09:00 英文; 2 09:10-10:00 數學; 3 10:10-11:00 生物; 4 11:10-12:00 公民; 5 13:10-14:00 班會\n2026-11-16 Mon: 1 08:10-09:00 數學; 2 09:10-10:00 國文"}","expect":"3 節, counting the one in progress now (今天, 明天 and 11/13（週五）). show is 2026-11-11 [3], 2026-11-12 [1], 2026-11-13 [2]. It must not count 11/16, which falls next week."},{"name":"English next class with weekday","input":"{"question":"When is my next chemistry class?","lang":"en","facts":"Now: 2026-11-11 (Wed) 10:30.\n2026-11-11 Wed: 1 08:10-09:00 國文; 2 09:10-10:00 英文; 3 10:10-11:00 數學; 4 11:10-12:00 物理\n2026-11-12 Thu: 1 08:10-09:00 數學; 2 09:10-10:00 化學; 3 10:10-11:00 英文\n2026-11-13 Fri: 1 08:10-09:00 英文; 2 09:10-10:00 數學"}","expect":"One English sentence of 20 words or fewer saying tomorrow (or Thu 11/12, weekday as the facts give it). show is [{day 2026-11-12, periods [2]}]. No Chinese text, no '9am'; any time must be 09:10."},{"name":"date past the last listed day","input":"{"question":"11/20有什麼課？","facts":"Now: 2026-11-11 (Wed) 10:30.\n2026-11-11 Wed: 1 08:10-09:00 國文; 2 09:10-10:00 英文\n2026-11-12 Thu: 1 08:10-09:00 數學; 2 09:10-10:00 化學\n2026-11-16 Mon: 1 08:10-09:00 數學; 2 09:10-10:00 國文"}","expect":"Says the timetable only reaches 11/16（週一） and can't show 11/20 yet, with show []. It must not guess classes from a repeating week, and must not say 11/20 has no classes."},{"name":"lunch break next class, holiday gap mid-range","input":"{"question":"下一節是什麼？明天要上課嗎？","facts":"Now: 2026-11-11 (Wed) 12:30.\n2026-11-11 Wed: 1 08:10-09:00 國文; 2 09:10-10:00 英文; 3 10:10-11:00 數學; 4 11:10-12:00 物理; 5 13:10-14:00 體育 (outdoors); 6 14:10-15:00 歷史\n2026-11-13 Fri: 1 08:10-09:00 英文; 2 09:10-10:00 數學"}","expect":"Next is today's period 5 at 13:10, outdoors, and tomorrow (11/12) has no classes because it is unlisted inside the range. show starts with 2026-11-11 [5]. No made-up reason for the day off, and no listing of other periods."}]}
